message: "This release is v0.2.0 (2026-10-09). Cite its own Zenodo version DOI after publication. The original July version DOI is recorded in docs/ARCHIVAL_PROVENANCE.md. Read paper/METHODOLOGICAL_CORRECTIONS_2026-10-09.md before interpreting historical findings."
title: "Does PCA Reveal or Fabricate Topological Structure in Omics Data? A Pre-Registered, Cross-Domain Replication with Matched Null Models"
authors:
  - family-names: Maniches
    given-names: Santiago
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6480-1987"
    affiliation: "TOPOLOGICA LLC"
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-09
abstract: "Computational research software and preserved evidence for cross-cohort PCA and persistent-homology analyses, including October 2026 post-preregistration statistical corrections and CPTAC follow-up null-model sensitivities. This release makes no claim of an established biological topology mechanism."
repository-code: "https://github.com/smaniches/pca-topology-crossdomain-replication"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - persistent homology
  - topological data analysis
  - principal component analysis
  - omics
  - pre-registration
  - confound analysis
